cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sloptrim: a deterministic prose-quality detector and always-on writing contract"
message: "If you use this software or its published measurements, please cite it. This is a pre-1.0 release; interfaces and score calibration may still change."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hadi
    given-names: Seyed Ehsan
repository-code: "https://github.com/seyedehsanhadi/sloptrim"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.9.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
keywords:
  - writing quality
  - text analysis
  - stylometry
  - large language models
  - research software
abstract: >-
  sloptrim is a deterministic local prose-pattern linter and writing contract.
  It documents 71 patterns, automates 62 of them, and reports which patterns
  occur without claiming who or what wrote the document. 50 can move the
  score; 12 are reported as writing advice. The runtime uses standard-library
  Python and Node.js and opens no network connection. On five public matched
  Human Detectors arms with 30 human and 30 machine articles each, its score
  achieved ROC-AUC 0.762 to 0.946. These are ranking results, not authorship or
  per-document accuracy claims. The benchmark's pinned source, aggregate results,
  confidence intervals, and offline reproduction harness ship with the repository.
